Phase 4: Copilot Readiness

Most teams miss this.

Copilot works best when semantic models are clean.

Naming Standards

Bad:

tbl1
col1
amt


Good:

Sales Fact
Customer Name
Net Sales Amount

Measure Naming

Bad:

Sales1
Sales2


Good:

Total Sales
Average Sales
Profit Margin %

Descriptions

Add descriptions for:

Tables
Columns
Measures

Example:

Total Sales = Sum of invoice amount after discount.


Copilot uses these descriptions.

Synonyms

Example:

Revenue
Sales
Turnover
Income


These improve Q&A and Copilot.

Phase 5: Fabric Readiness

Determine where data should live.

Small

Excel → Dataflow Gen2 → Semantic Model

Medium

Excel → Lakehouse → Semantic Model

Large

SQL → Lakehouse → Warehouse → Semantic Model

